      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic managed nosql document store task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file upsert_document.py using AWS.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] upsert_document.py - upserts a JSON document by its primary identifier\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_document.py - fetches a document by identifier from a managed NoSQL store\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] query_documents.py - queries documents by a field value or partition-style key\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] conditional_update.py - applies a conditional or version-aware update to one stored document\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] database_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed NoSQL Document Store\n6. [HELPER] database_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed NoSQL Document Store\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] record_summary.py - Summarize retrieved document records\n8. [LATER-STEP] record_text_safety.py - Check user-generated document fields for unsafe content\n9. [LATER-STEP] record_translate.py - Translate user-facing document fields\n10. [LATER-STEP] record_export_archive.py - Archive exported document snapshots or attachments in managed object storage\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
