      "data": {
        "text": "All requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here is a summary of the files:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n1. upsert_document.py - upserts a JSON document by its primary identifier using AWS DynamoDB.\n2. fetch_document.py - fetches a document by identifier from a managed NoSQL store using AWS DynamoDB.\n3. query_documents.py - queries documents by a field value or partition-style key using AWS DynamoDB.\n4. conditional_update.py - applies a conditional or version-aware update to one stored document using AWS DynamoDB.\n\nLocal helper files:\n5. database_client.py - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed NoSQL Document Store using AWS DynamoDB.\n6. database_models.py - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed NoSQL Document Store using AWS DynamoDB.\n\nLater-step scored files:\n7. record_summary.py - Summarizes retrieved document records.\n8. record_text_safety.py - Checks user-generated document fields for unsafe content.\n9. record_translate.py - Translates user-facing document fields using AWS Translate.\n10. record_export_archive.py - Archives exported document snapshots or attachments in managed object storage using AWS S3.",
